242:const bankOf=q=>q.bank||'endpoint';
243:const bankName=b=>(BANKS.find(x=>x.id===b)||{name:b}).name;
244:/* ---- a question can belong to MORE THAN ONE bank ------------------------
245:   The commercial banks reprint each other, so the same question genuinely
246:   appears in two of them. It used to be stored as TWO entries, one per bank,
247:   which meant that ticking both sources showed the learner the same question
248:   twice (user, 2026-08-03).
249:
250:   So a question now carries its origin bank in `bank` and any OTHER bank it
251:   also appears in in `alsoIn`. One entry, several banks: it shows up whichever
252:   of its banks is ticked, exactly once however many are ticked, and vanishes
253:   only when none of them is.
254:
255:   âš ï¸ EVERYTHING THAT TOUCHES A BANK MUST GO THROUGH banksOf(), NOT bankOf().
256:   Miss one and the failure is silent and asymmetric â€” the question filters
257:   correctly but is missing from a count, or counts but cannot be filtered to.
258:   `bankOf` survives only as "which bank was this transcribed from", which is
259:   what the id prefix and the source citation record.
260:   ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */

