+# P1b — sync correctness design
+
+Scope: P1 exit conditions only. Keep classic scripts, vanilla JS, `file://` and
+offline use; Firebase stays optional. Do not rename any `wardround.*` key.
+
+## Evidence: present behaviour
+
+| Concern | Today | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| Six maps | `mergeStates` overlays whole maps selected by `updatedAt`; no entry clocks. | `app/js/gate.js:202-223` |
+| Confidence | `setConf` writes `conf`, and sometimes `srs`, without a timestamp. | `app/js/quiz.js:527-537` |
+| Schedule marks | Keys are `date|array-index`; deleting splices and renumbers them. | `app/js/sessions.js:334-349` |
+| Deletes | Highlight delete is a plain `delete`; day delete deletes marks; profile delete removes only live state. | `app/js/quiz.js:1004`; `app/js/sessions.js:361-367`; `app/js/gate.js:906-914` |
+| Cloud input | Cloud `JSON.parse` goes straight to merge, whereas import calls `checkedProgressState`. | `app/js/gate.js:287-290`; `app/js/boot.js:273-284` |
+| Ownership/sign-out | Every local profile syncs under current account; sign-out catches and discards error. | `app/js/gate.js:135-140`, `753-755` |
+| CDN | Dynamic script loader has timeout but attaches no `integrity`. | `app/js/gate.js:11-31` |
+| Recovery | `loadState` only restores backup after missing/unparseable live state. | `app/js/storage.js:47-75` |
+
+## Wire format and merge
+
+Add `syncV:1`, `deviceId` (random durable per installation), `clock` (last issued
+millisecond), and `records` to a state. `records[k][id]` is an envelope:
+`{v:<existing value>, c:[wallMs,deviceId], del?:true}`. `k` is exactly `srs`,
+`hl`, `flags`, `conf`, `days`, or `sched`. Values remain materialised in the
+existing six maps for current readers; envelopes are canonical sync metadata.
+
+`tick()` returns `[max(Date.now(), S.clock+1), deviceId]`, updates `S.clock`, and
+is called by one `putRecord(k,id,value)` or `deleteRecord(k,id)` helper before
+every `save()`: quiz SRS/conf/flag/highlight writes, all highlight removal, and
+schedule mark/day/item/whole-plan changes. The helper updates both map and
+envelope; delete removes the materialised map entry and writes `del:true`.
+`migrateSched()` must use the helper only after legacy conversion.
+
+For a record present on both sides, choose lexicographically greatest `c`
+(`wallMs`, then opaque `deviceId` byte order); tombstone is an ordinary winner.
+Thus equal clocks are deterministic in either merge direction. Clocks are
+client wall time, not trusted chronology: a clock behind advances locally via
+`max`; a clock far ahead wins until another write exceeds it. Show one nonfatal
+"device clock differs; latest sync follows its clock" notice per session when
+incoming wall time is >24 h ahead/behind local time; never rewrite received
+clocks. State-level settings retain their current explicit rules unless moved to
+records later.
+
+`schedule` item shape becomes `{id,label,text,hex}`; id is `deviceId + '-' +
+tick()[0]` at creation and is never regenerated. Mark key is `date+'|'+item.id`.
+Render/edit/delete by id, not index. A legacy item gets an id once during
+migration; legacy `date|index` marks are translated in the same in-memory
+transaction. A deleted item records a `sched` tombstone; deleted day/reset
+records tombstones for every contained stable mark/item. Do not renumber.
+
+Notes join the same envelope/tombstone mechanism (although already individually
+timestamped: `app/js/gate.js:232-242`); highlights are one record per question.
+Profiles use `{id,ownerUid|null,...,c,del?:true}` in a separately merged roster.
+Profile, note, highlight and schedule tombstones live 90 days after their winning
+clock, then GC only during a successful authenticated transaction after merging
+both sides. Never GC offline or local-only; deletion wins throughout retention.
+
+## Cloud, validation, ownership
+
+Extract `parseProgressState(raw)` in `boot.js`: JSON parse then
+`checkedProgressState`; import and every cloud read call this exact function.
+Extend `checkedProgressState` for `syncV`, clock/envelopes/tombstones, stable
+schedule ids, and profile owner fields; preserve unrelated forward fields as it
+does today (`app/js/boot.js:197-264`). Invalid cloud state is not merged or
+written back: set sync error with "Cloud progress was not accepted" and retain
+local state.
+
+Use canonical child document `users/{uid}/profiles/{pid}/sync/v1`, containing
+the validated state. Keep the existing profile document's `state` as a legacy
+bridge only: old clients cannot erase the child document by their whole-document
+`set` (`app/js/gate.js:291`). Canonical state stores `legacyAppliedAt`; new client
+imports legacy state only when its `updatedAt` is later, normalises it, then
+advances that marker. This makes an old client's later legacy write observable
+without allowing it to destroy record clocks/tombstones. New clients never use
+legacy state as canonical after migration.
+
+On profile creation while signed in set `ownerUid=fbUser.uid`; cloud roster and
+document operations require equality. On account switch, profiles owned by the
+other UID remain device-only and cannot auto-upload. An `ownerUid:null` profile
+shows a choice: "Upload to <account>" (sets owner, explicit action) or "Keep on
+this device". No implicit adoption. Sign-out modal offers "remove account data
+from this device" (remove only profiles owned by that UID plus their live and
+`wardround.bak.<profileId>` keys); report each local removal failure and do not
+claim completion. `signOutCloud` must surface Firebase sign-out failure rather
+than swallow it (`app/js/gate.js:139`).
+
+Profile delete: first write its roster tombstone and delete cloud profile/sync
+documents in a bounded transaction/batch; only then remove local profile, live
+key, and `wardround.bak.<profileId>`. If cloud delete fails, keep local data and
+show retryable "Cloud profile delete failed"; never toast success. Local storage
+failures are likewise surfaced.
+
+Pin exact, versioned Firebase CDN URLs and SHA-384 `integrity` values in the
+`SDK` list; set `crossOrigin='anonymous'` before append. Preserve `loadSDK()`'s
+8 s timeout and `boot()` 15 s race/local-only fallback.
+
+## Migration and compatibility
+
+`syncV:1` is the marker. First new-client load of state without it assigns one
+`tick()` clock to every extant record (same millisecond, device-id tie breaker),
+creates no tombstones, assigns schedule ids/translates marks, validates, then
+atomically saves local state before its first cloud push. If save fails, retain
+legacy in memory, warn through existing persistent-save warning, and do not
+publish migration. Re-running is idempotent; interruption before the save simply
+restarts; after save recognises `syncV:1`.
+
+Never delete/rename live or backup `wardround.*` keys. `loadState` retains its
+missing/unparseable-only rescue contract. Old client compatibility is via the
+child canonical document and legacy bridge above; a newer state is not placed
+only in the old whole-state field. An old client may lose its own unsupported
+metadata in legacy state, but cannot remove canonical v1 data; its subsequent
+legacy progress is imported by `legacyAppliedAt`.
+
+## Acceptance checks
+
+| Case | Concrete check | Device requirement |
+|---|---|---|
+| Real auth | Two browser profiles sign into a real test Firebase account, independently edit same/different records, force push/pull; assert record winner/tombstone and UID isolation. | Real network/account |
+| Popup/redirect blocked | Stub popup rejection `popup-blocked`, assert redirect call and retained local gate; standalone path asserts redirect. | iOS standalone redirect needs real iOS Safari |
+| Account switch | A-owned profile under B has no cloud write; unlinked prompt requires explicit Upload; choose Keep and assert no write. | Scriptable with mocked Firebase; real auth smoke |
+| Offline restart | Block network, write, close/reopen; assert local state and backup recovery rules; reconnect then merge. | Scriptable; iOS/Android real smoke |
+| Storage failure | Throw on `setItem`/storage.set; assert warning, no false success, download offered, memory remains usable. | Scriptable |
+| Migration interruption | Seed v0, interrupt before/after local migration save; restart and assert one stable-id mapping/no loss/no duplicate clocks. | Scriptable |
+| SW update | Serve old shell then activate updated worker mid-queued push; reload and assert canonical record/tombstone survives. | Scriptable desktop; real iOS Safari and Android browser/PWA |
+
+Run the scripted cases in current Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari desktop; manually
+run real-auth, redirect, offline restart, and SW-update cases on iOS Safari and
+Android Chrome (including installed PWA where supported). `app/smoke.html` may
+host deterministic fake clock/storage/Firebase tests; real auth and device/SW
+behaviour cannot be fully scripted there.
+
+## Ordered build split
+
+1. Validator/parser plus v0→v1 local migration and stable schedule ids. Check:
+   fixture validation, idempotent interrupted migration, `file://` boot.
+2. Record helpers and all six-map/note/schedule write paths; deterministic merge.
+   Check: two-state merge matrix, delete-vs-write/tie/skew tests.
+3. Canonical child cloud document, legacy bridge, invalid-cloud rejection and
+   SRI. Check: transaction fixtures, old-client bridge fixture, 8 s/15 s fallbacks.
+4. Ownership, roster tombstones, profile/sign-out deletion UX. Check: UID switch,
+   unlinked choice, cloud/local delete failure assertions.
+5. Smoke harness and browser/device matrix. Check: every acceptance row recorded
+   against the named browser/version/device.
+
+## Open questions for the owner
+
+- Is 90 days the desired tombstone retention period, or should it be longer?
+- Should "remove account data from this device" remove only cloud-owned profiles
+  or also their backups when a local storage removal error leaves a partial result?

