+| Migration interruption | Seed v0, interrupt before/after local migration save; restart and assert one stable-id mapping/no loss/no duplicate clocks. | Scriptable |
+| SW update | Serve old shell then activate updated worker mid-queued push; reload and assert canonical record/tombstone survives. | Scriptable desktop; real iOS Safari and Android browser/PWA |
+
+Run the scripted cases in current Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari desktop; manually
+run real-auth, redirect, offline restart, and SW-update cases on iOS Safari and
+Android Chrome (including installed PWA where supported). `app/smoke.html` may
+host deterministic fake clock/storage/Firebase tests; real auth and device/SW
+behaviour cannot be fully scripted there.
+
+## Ordered build split
+
+1. Validator/parser plus v0→v1 local migration and stable schedule ids. Check:
+   fixture validation, idempotent interrupted migration, `file://` boot.
+2. Record helpers and all six-map/note/schedule write paths; deterministic merge.
+   Check: two-state merge matrix, delete-vs-write/tie/skew tests.
+3. Canonical child cloud document, legacy bridge, invalid-cloud rejection and
+   SRI. Check: transaction fixtures, old-client bridge fixture, 8 s/15 s fallbacks.
+4. Ownership, roster tombstones, profile/sign-out deletion UX. Check: UID switch,
+   unlinked choice, cloud/local delete failure assertions.
+5. Smoke harness and browser/device matrix. Check: every acceptance row recorded
+   against the named browser/version/device.
+
+## Open questions for the owner
+
+- Is 90 days the desired tombstone retention period, or should it be longer?
+- Should "remove account data from this device" remove only cloud-owned profiles
+  or also their backups when a local storage removal error leaves a partial result?

